  "comments": [
    {"at":0,"placement":"line","text":"Repeats hit_test until hit_code is not 0. Then it subtracts the table bytes at hit_cell_ptr + Y - 2 and + Y - 4 from cursor_x and cursor_y, and returns A = hit_code. Only the jump table entry $0903 points to it; the runs did not execute it."},
    {"at":31,"placement":"line","text":"4 bytes that nothing executes. As code they are LDA $F0, BEQ $1C85."},
    {"at":37,"placement":"line","text":"Finds the cell under the cursor (hit_lookup), then moves the cursor sprites (move_cursor_sprites). hit_code gets the code of the cell, or 0."},
    {"at":43,"placement":"line","text":"Reads the cursor (read_cursor) and looks for the cell that holds cursor_x, cursor_y in the table at hit_table_ptr: count, then 5 bytes for each cell (Y max, Y min, X end, X min, code). hit_code gets the code of the first cell that matches, or 0. No table (hit_table_ptr = 0) gives 0."}
  ],
